{
"dur": 41.773,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 8.6,
"text": "So when Twilight wrapped in 2012, he did the opposite of what a heartthrob is supposed to do. He went looking for the strangest directors he could find.",
"end": 8.875
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.875,
"vo_start": 9.15,
"vo_end": 18.11,
"text": "David Cronenberg, twice. James Gray. Claire Denis. Small films, odd films, films that most of his fans never saw.",
"end": 18.385
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.385,
"vo_start": 18.66,
"vo_end": 29.78,
"text": "The turning point was a film called Good Time in 2017. He played a desperate small-time crook running through New York for one terrible night, and critics finally said it out loud. This man can act.",
"end": 30.055
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 30.055,
"vo_start": 30.33,
"vo_end": 40.823,
"text": "Then came The Lighthouse, where he and Willem Dafoe slowly lose their minds on a rock in the sea. Then Christopher Nolan cast him in Tenet, in a sharp suit, doing spy work. Sound familiar?",
"end": 41.773
}
],
